[ceiling] Each flat pull roof is a hand-contact face at nominal Z272.194, including the 0.25 mm supported-face allowance. The added exterior transition joins this bearing without replacing it with a slope. Left support can exit toward -X and right support toward +X through the exposed mouths before pumps are installed. The current geometry requires a fresh native support-contact review and physical removal check.
alternatives: Replacing the roof with a ramp changes the flat lifting contact and reduces finger room. Closing the recess removes the hand pull. The flat lifting surface retains its required shape and receives supports through the exposed side mouth; geometric access does not establish removal quality.
