[step] Required side-groove engagement of the purchased SB443-IN blocks. Each rail projects 0.700 mm into the 6.650 mm slot, ending 2.625 mm from the column axis. The common full-tolerance groove neck leaves 0.1104 mm nominal radial air at the rail tips. This step is the magnet's positive capture interface; mechanically keyed cured fill takes up its actual groove allowance. magnet-geometry.json binds the supplier envelope, loading route and positive keyed retention. Printed fit and joint strength remain unqualified.
alternatives: Removing the projection eliminates the groove's positive capture. Moving the tips inward reduces the worst-drawing neck clearance. Widening the slot reduces engagement or requires wider columns and their matching fixed-wall recesses. A separate screw cap would add retention parts and factory assembly operations. The present narrow interface is specific to the purchased grooved block.
