[sliver] Required SB443-IN groove rails, 0.600 mm in Y and 0.700 mm in X. The full supplier tolerance leaves a common Y groove interval only 0.8382 mm wide, from 1.8542 to 2.6924 mm behind the pole. The rail occupies 2.000–2.600 mm and joins the side-key cavity at its back face. The cured keyed fill is part of the joint and closes its axial and vertical loading allowances. This is a purchased-part retention exception to ordinary 3 mm walls, with no printed-strength claim.
alternatives: A 3 mm rail cannot enter the supplier groove. Extending the rail toward either groove face consumes the recorded supplier clearance; widening its X projection consumes groove-neck clearance. Removing it leaves adhesion as the axial capture. A differently grooved block or a separate bolted retainer changes the purchased interface or adds assembly parts. The current rails retain their explicit fit and physical-qualification limits.
