[ceiling] Flat closure above each front-loading magnet mouth and its cured side keys. The 3 mm roof preserves the full supplier block-loading headroom below the retained pump-skirt support band at Z206.674. It also closes the cured fill's positive-Z route. The empty mouth opens toward +Y, so automatic supports can leave through that opening before magnet installation. Access alone does not establish support removal or roof finish.
alternatives: A ramp into the cavity obstructs the full-height loading envelope. Raising a 45° roof over the 9.85 mm key span carries its cavity crest above Z207.780, into the retained skirt-support band and its 3 mm aft stock. Opening the roof removes the fill's Z closure. The flat roof preserves both fitted interfaces and receives support through the empty loading mouth.
