alternatives: Cutting a 45° underside inside the present envelope reduces its 3 mm floor to 1.15 mm at the proud edge. Adding a downward supporting wedge preserves that floor but requires a larger fixed-wall recess below the retained guard envelope. The flat floor keeps the defined capture stock and fitted recess; accessible supports retain the required shape.
